---

A Virtual Private Cloud (VPC) is a secure, isolated private network hosted within a public cloud provider's infrastructure. It provides customizable networking components—such as subnets, route tables, and gateways—allowing businesses to securely run resources like virtual machines (e.g., EC2) and databases in a dedicated environment.

